ation": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Identical quote parameters succeeded after transient failures, so recovery retries only estimation once; persistent provider failure stops with amount-specific guidance and never broadens signing authority."}, {"id": "docs_project_map_swap_stop_limit", "label": "Public Swap Kit stopLimit uses human-readable EURC; stored minima and Circle HTTP stopLimit use integer base units", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_MAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The incorrect 8a5f400 change passed stored integers to the public SDK, whose resolveSwapConfig scaled them again. Format the stored six-decimal minimum as a human-readable amount before SwapKit.swap/estimate; the SDK restores exactly the approved integer for Circle.", "description": "Stored 2455668 \u2192 formatUnits(minimum, 6) \u2192 public SDK 2.455668 \u2192 resolveSwapConfig \u2192 Circle HTTP 2455668. Passing public SDK 2455668 instead emitted 2455668000000. Stored quote minima and receipt verification remain integers; retain 100-bps slippage."}, {"id": "docs_project_map_quote_http_fixture_tests", "label": "Installed SDK HTTP-fixture regressions exercise real wire requests, base-unit conversion and Circle error parsing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/PROJECT_MAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "description": "Three SwapKit.swap HTTP-boundary tests use real installed parameter resolution, reject the provider response before approval/signing, and cover 3-USDC, sub-EURC, and one-micro-EURC floors. Replace the mocked swap test that reinforced incorrect stop-limit units. Quote recovery fixtures also exercise installed SDK request/error parsing."}, {"id": "docs_project_map_testnet_route", "label": "Base \u2192 CCTP \u2192 